  closing:(s,all,G)=>{const p=s.picks||{}, ta=G.r_testarticle, ct=G.crashedtest, spun=s.flags.spunmedia;
    return [
    `Thursday, November 9. 10:40 PM. The workaround's ground runs had gone on at night all week, because the cell and its people were cheaper at night and Wendell was better. They were running `+(ta?`at Stand 2, on the second test article, trucked out from Building 6 for the long soaks, the valve that had done more cold cycles than any in history,`:`at Stand 2, on the lot sample valve Aldergrove had trucked up from Pueblo in October,`)+` and Sam was in the blockhouse with Quinn, because he'd started coming out for them and couldn't have said why.`,
    (p[7]===2
      ?`The load was the one the board had approved, verified line by line, and nothing else. Rafa's pulse was on the change board's agenda for Tuesday, with a test written for it.`
      :p[7]===0
        ?`The load still had Rafa's pulse in it. Thandi had stopped saying so out loud and started writing it down.`
        :p[7]===1
          ?`The load was the approved one. The pulse had come out without a record, and somebody on Rafa's team was still asking what had happened to it.`
          :`The load was the approved one, and Rafa's team had stopped bringing Sam their ideas.`),
    `The month was on a sheet in his notebook. `+(p[1]===3&&!spun
        ?`Frances's call was Friday at ten, the fifth one. She'd started them by reading out what the families were hearing, so he'd know what to correct.`
        :spun
          ?`Greaves had put the word history on a graphic and used it every night for a week. Frances took Sam's calls now, and answered them in full sentences, which was worse than not answering.`
          :`Frances took his calls. She took Greaves's too.`)
      +(p[6]===0?` Kittiwake had written to say it would bid on the station's resupply.`:``)
      +(p[9]===0?` Launch 3 was a week out, on the 16th, bought back a day at a time.`:p[9]===2?` Launch 3 had moved to the 30th.`:` Launch 3's date was a question Quinn answered differently every morning.`),
    `He'd answered Ada's log forty three the night he got home, at the kitchen table, in his own chair. `+(spun
        ?`It had taken him four tries. He'd told her history was the wrong word and that he'd known it when he said it.`
        :p[0]===0
          ?`He'd told her what he should have told Greaves, and about the gray bar down the side of the scan.`
          :`He'd told her what he'd told Greaves, and the part he hadn't, about the gray bar down the side of the scan.`),
    (s.score>=27
      ?`Quinn had pinned October's five asks to the wall, one sheet each, and a sixth beside them, blank except for a date at the top. She said it was for whatever walked in next.`
      :`It had been `+(ct?`six`:`five`)+` weeks of the outside walking in, and he could name the doors he'd let it through that he shouldn't have. Knowing them was most of what Ruth's pages were for.`),
    `Cycle after cycle came back under four milliseconds, with the conditioning cycle ahead of the close and MOIV-2 shutting behind it like a second hand on a door. Twice, on the third cycle after a long soak, the trace showed a small ripple about two milliseconds after the poppet lifted.`+(ct?``:` Sam had seen that ripple once before, at the Cape, in September, beside a seven.`),
    `At 10:52 Wendell stood up from the propulsion console to look at something on the far screen, put his hand out for the back of the chair, and missed it.`,
    `Quinn got to him first. He was on the blockhouse floor on his side, awake, saying he was fine in a voice that wasn't. Arlo called it in from the stand. The ambulance came up the gravel road with its lights on and no siren, because Arlo had told them there was nobody out there to wake, and the pronghorn in the ditch didn't move.`,
    `At 2:10 AM a doctor at the hospital in Aurora said low blood pressure, and a heart that needed a better look, and that he was fine for tonight. They also said that seventy one year old men shouldn't be working nights on a prairie in November. Wendell said he'd been told.`,
    `Sam sat in the chair by the bed with his jacket still on. Wendell looked at the ceiling for a while.`,
    `<span class="said" data-who="Wendell">"This is the last one, Sam. I'll see it to December. Then I'm done. I've been done since 2035. I kept forgetting."</span>`,
    `Sam didn't argue. He thought about what was in that bed. How a seat sounded when it was lying. Which ripple was ice and which wasn't. The thing Wendell had heard in 2034, and in 2059, and at 10:52 tonight, when he'd stood up to look. Some of it was in procedures now. The part that mattered had never been written down by anybody, because nobody had ever asked him the right way, and he'd never offered.`,
  ].filter(x=>x!==``);},
